Below is a quick-reference guide that shows **all the practical ways you can add a search / geocoder box to a Mapbox GL JS v2 map** – from the official Mapbox-provided widget to fully open-source alternatives that work with any tile source.  
For each option I list:

| Option | Who provides it | What you need (API key, server, etc.) | How to plug it into a Mapbox GL JS v2 map (code snippet) | Pros | Cons / Caveats |
|--------|----------------|----------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------|------|----------------|
| **Mapbox Geocoder plugin** (`@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder`) | Mapbox | **Mapbox access token** (same token you use for the map) | See snippet below | • Tight integration (auto-adds results as a source/layer) <br>• Handles address, POI, and reverse-geocode <br>• Fully styled, mobile-friendly UI | • Requires a Mapbox token → you pay per request after the free tier <br>• Tied to Mapbox’s Geocoding API (no self-host) |
| **Mapbox Search SDK (Web)** (`@mapbox/search-js`) | Mapbox | **Mapbox Search API key** (different from the map token) | See snippet below | • Newer, more flexible UI (autocomplete, fuzzy search) <br>• Supports “search-as-you-type” and “search-by-category” <br>• Works with Mapbox GL JS v2+ | • Still a paid service (free tier limited) <br>• Slightly larger bundle than the classic geocoder |
| **MapLibre-GL-Geocoder** (`@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder`) | Open-source community (MapLibre) | Any geocoding endpoint you like (Nominatim, Photon, Pelias, MapTiler, etc.) | See snippet below | • No Mapbox token required <br>• Works with Mapbox GL JS v2 because the UI is just a plain HTML widget that adds a source/layer <br>• You can point it at any HTTP-based geocoder (including self-hosted) | • You must provide your own geocoder service (or use a free public one) <br>• UI is a bit more “bare-bones” – you may need to style it yourself |
| **Algolia Places** (deprecated, still usable) | Algolia | Free Algolia API key (public) | See snippet below | • Very fast, client-side index <br>• No per-request cost (free tier) | • Project is no longer actively maintained (no new data) <br>• Limited to places that Algolia indexed (mostly major cities) |
| **OpenStreetMap Nominatim** (public or self-hosted) | OSM community | No key for the public demo (rate-limited) – you should self-host or use a managed provider for production | Use any of the UI wrappers (MapLibre-GL-Geocoder, custom fetch + dropdown) | • 100 % open data, free to self-host <br>• Gives you full control over usage limits | • Public demo (`https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org`) is **not** for production (strict rate limits, mandatory attribution) <br>• You need to handle CORS or proxy if you self-host |
| **Photon** (by Komoot) | Open-source (Komoot) | Public endpoint (`https://photon.komoot.io`) – free but rate-limited; self-hostable | Same UI wrappers as above | • Fast, lightweight Elasticsearch-based index <br>• Good for POI search | • Public endpoint is rate-limited; you’ll likely self-host for production |
| **Pelias** (open-source) | Mapzen / community | Self-host or use a managed service (e.g., MapTiler Geocoding) | Same UI wrappers | • Highly configurable (multiple data sources, custom ranking) | • Requires more infrastructure to run yourself |
| **MapTiler Geocoding** (commercial, but free tier) | MapTiler | API key from MapTiler Cloud | Same UI wrappers (just change the endpoint) | • Simple pricing, generous free tier (up to 100 k requests/mo) <br>• Works with any Mapbox-style map | • Not free beyond the tier; you need a MapTiler account |
| **Custom UI + Direct API Calls** | Anything | Any HTTP geocoder (including the ones above) | Build your own `<input>` + fetch → results → `map.flyTo()` | • Full control over UI/UX, can combine multiple services | • More code to maintain, you lose the “auto-add source/layer” convenience |

Below you’ll find **ready-to-copy code snippets** for the most common scenarios, plus a short “how-to-choose” decision matrix.

---

## 1️⃣ Official Mapbox Geocoder plugin (the simplest, most common)

```bash
# Install the plugin (v5.x works with Mapbox GL JS v2)
npm i @mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder
# or via CDN:
# <script src="https://api.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/plugins/mapbox-gl-geocoder/v5.0.1/mapbox-gl-geocoder.min.js"></script>
# <link href="https://api.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/plugins/mapbox-gl-geocoder/v5.0.1/mapbox-gl-geocoder.css" rel="stylesheet" />
```

```javascript
import mapboxgl from 'mapbox-gl';
import MapboxGeocoder from '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder';
import '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder/dist/mapbox-gl-geocoder.css';

// Your Mapbox token (required for both the map and the geocoder)
mapboxgl.accessToken = 'YOUR_MAPBOX_ACCESS_TOKEN';

const map = new mapboxgl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'mapbox://styles/mapbox/streets-v12',
  center: [-122.42, 37.78],
  zoom: 12
});

// Add the geocoder UI
const geocoder = new MapboxGeocoder({
  accessToken: mapboxgl.accessToken,
  mapboxgl: mapboxgl,          // required to use the built-in result marker
  placeholder: 'Search places…',
  // optional: limit results to a country or bounding box
  // countries: 'us',
  // bbox: [-124.848974, 24.396308, -66.885444, 49.384358]
});

map.addControl(geocoder, 'top-left');   // position can be 'top-left', 'top-right', etc.
```

**What you get out of the box**

| Feature | Details |
|---------|---------|
| **Result marker** – a default pin is added to the map automatically. |
| **Fly-to animation** – the map animates to the selected result. |
| **Reverse-geocode on click** – you can enable `reverseGeocode: true` to let the user click the map and get an address. |
| **Keyboard navigation** – arrow keys move through the dropdown. |
| **Internationalization** – set `language: 'fr'` etc. |
| **Proximity bias** – `proximity: {longitude, latitude}` can be set to favor results near the user. |

**Cost & limits** (as of 2026-10)

| Tier | Free requests / month | Price per 1 000 extra requests |
|------|----------------------|--------------------------------|
| Free | 100 000 (Geocoding API) | $0.50 |
| Pay-as-you-go | – | $0.50 per 1 000 (after free tier) |

> **Tip:** If you already have a Mapbox token for the map, you can reuse it for the geocoder. If you want to keep the map token public (e.g., in a client-side bundle) but hide the geocoder key, you can create a **restricted token** that only has the `geocoding:search` scope.

---

## 2️⃣ Mapbox Search SDK (newer, richer UI)

The Search SDK is a **separate product** from the classic Geocoder. It offers a modern autocomplete UI, category filters, and “search-as-you-type” that can be embedded directly in any page.

```bash
npm i @mapbox/search-js @mapbox/search-js-react   # React wrapper optional
```

```javascript
import mapboxgl from 'mapbox-gl';
import { SearchBox } from '@mapbox/search-js';
import '@mapbox/search-js/dist/search-js.css';

mapboxgl.accessToken = 'YOUR_MAPBOX_ACCESS_TOKEN';

const map = new mapboxgl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'mapbox://styles/mapbox/streets-v12',
  center: [-122.42, 37.78],
  zoom: 12
});

// Create a SearchBox instance
const searchBox = new SearchBox({
  accessToken: 'YOUR_MAPBOX_SEARCH_API_KEY', // can be the same token but you may want a separate one
  container: 'search-container',            // any empty div in your HTML
  placeholder: 'Search places…',
  // optional: limit to a country, set proximity, etc.
  // countries: ['us'],
  // proximity: { longitude: -122.42, latitude: 37.78 }
});

searchBox.on('result', (event) => {
  const { result } = event; // result is a GeoJSON Feature
  map.flyTo({ center: result.geometry.coordinates, zoom: 14 });
});
```

**Why you might pick this over the classic plugin**

| Feature | Search SDK | Classic Geocoder |
|---------|------------|------------------|
| **Autocomplete** (type-ahead) | ✅ (fast, fuzzy) | ✅ (but older UI) |
| **Category filters** (e.g., “restaurants”) | ✅ | ❌ |
| **Custom result rendering** (you can supply your own HTML) | ✅ | Limited |
| **React / Vue wrappers** | ✅ (`@mapbox/search-js-react`) | No official wrappers |
| **Bundle size** | Slightly larger (≈ 30 KB gz) | Smaller (≈ 15 KB gz) |
| **Pricing** | Same Geocoding API pricing (free tier 100 k) | Same |

If you already use Mapbox Search elsewhere (e.g., in a mobile app) you’ll probably want the SDK for consistency.

---

## 3️⃣ Open-source UI + Open Geocoder (self-host or free public endpoint)

If you **don’t want to pay Mapbox** (or you’re already planning to move to a non-Mapbox tile source), you can keep the same UI component (`@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder`) and point it at any HTTP geocoder that returns **GeoJSON FeatureCollection** in the Mapbox-compatible format.

### 3.1 Install the UI component

```bash
npm i @maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder
# or via CDN:
# <script src="https://unpkg.com/@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder@latest/dist/maplibre-gl-geocoder.min.js"></script>
# <link href="https://unpkg.com/@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder@latest/dist/maplibre-gl-geocoder.css" rel="stylesheet" />
```

### 3.2 Example using **OpenStreetMap Nominatim** (public demo – *not* for production)

```javascript
import mapboxgl from 'mapbox-gl';          // you can keep using Mapbox GL JS v2
import MapLibreGeocoder from '@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder';
import '@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder/dist/maplibre-gl-geocoder.css';

mapboxgl.accessToken = 'YOUR_MAPBOX_TOKEN'; // only needed for the map itself

const map = new mapboxgl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'mapbox://styles/mapbox/streets-v12',
  center: [-122.42, 37.78],
  zoom: 12
});

const geocoder = new MapLibreGeocoder({
  // Nominatim returns results in the same shape Mapbox expects (Feature with geometry)
  // The `url` option overrides the default Mapbox endpoint.
  url: 'https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search?format=geojson&addressdetails=1',
  // Optional: add a `params` object for static query parameters (e.g., `countrycodes=us`)
  // params: { countrycodes: 'us' },
  placeholder: 'Search OSM…',
  // If you want to add a custom marker, set `marker: false` and handle it
